s3presign — startup `RunOnce` plus 12-hour `time.Ticker` loop  
webhook async dispatch (4 workers) — channel queue (`asyncPostQueue`) fed by `PostAsync` on webhook events  

**Unused infrastructure:** `internal/scheduler` (cron job scheduler in `internal/scheduler/`) is not imported or started by the server. `memopayload.Runner` in `server/runner/memopayload/runner.go` is never started; only `RebuildMemoPayload` runs inline on memo create/update.

The server explicitly starts background runners in `startBackgroundRunners` in `server/server.go`:

```153:171:server/server.go
func (s *Server) startBackgroundRunners(ctx context.Context) {
	// ...
	s3presignRunner := s3presign.NewRunner(s.Store)
	s3presignRunner.RunOnce(ctx)

	s.backgroundRunnerWG.Add(1)
	go func() {
		defer s.backgroundRunnerWG.Done()
		s3presignRunner.Run(s3Context)
		slog.Info("s3presign runner stopped")
	}()
```

The s3presign runner runs once at startup, then on a 12-hour ticker:

```26:40:server/runner/s3presign/runner.go
// Schedule runner every 12 hours.
const runnerInterval = time.Hour * 12

func (r *Runner) Run(ctx context.Context) {
	ticker := time.NewTicker(runnerInterval)
	defer ticker.Stop()

	for {
		select {
		case <-ticker.C:
			r.RunOnce(ctx)
		case <-ctx.Done():
			return
		}
	}
}
```

Webhook delivery uses four background goroutines started in `init()` in `internal/webhook/webhook.go` when the package is loaded (via `cmd/memos/main.go` and API webhook handlers). They read from `asyncPostQueue` when handlers call `PostAsync` — event-driven, not scheduled.

The cron scheduler in `internal/scheduler/` (see `internal/scheduler/doc.go`) is only referenced from its own tests/examples, not from `server/` or `cmd/`.

